<title>USA: U.S. durables orders rose in April.</title>
<headline>U.S. durables orders rose in April.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Strong demand for new transportation equipment helped drive orders for costly manufactured goods up in April, the Commerce Department said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The total value of new orders for durable goods rose 1.4 percent to a seasonally adjusted $175.56 billion -- a third increase in the past four months -- following a revised 2.2 percent drop in March.</p>
